    "narrative": "Heading into today\u2019s slate, **Tyler Freeman** (66.24) stands out as our premier start. Facing Eric Lauer, **Freeman** benefits from an elite matchup against a struggling arm (5.28 xERA) and a prime spot in the heart of the order (#4), maximizing his potential for RBI and run production. Joining him as high-ceiling plays are **Daulton Varsho** (59.41) and **Yainer Diaz** (59.26). **Varsho** is particularly intriguing; while his matchup against Landen Roupp is neutral, the combination of a positive wind factor and his dynamic platoon advantage against right-handed pitching elevates his floor significantly. Even with the defensive threat of an elite catcher, **Varsho** remains a core piece for our offensive output today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the morning was balancing the bench, specifically regarding the utility slot where **Luis Arraez** (55.31) edged out our other options. While **Arraez** faces a formidable arm in Kevin Gausman, his leadoff placement (#1) provides a massive +10% boost to his efficiency, making him a more reliable source of base hits and runs than our deeper bench reserves. We are keeping a close eye on **Drew Gilbert** (43.35) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (52.62), both of whom also draw the Gausman assignment; the wind blowing out is the only reason they remain in starting consideration, acting as a hedge against the strikeout risk inherent in facing a pitcher of that caliber. \n\nOwners should be aware that all scores are currently based on projected lineups; a late shift in batting order could see players like **Masyn Winn** (42.49) or **Bryson Stott** (47.77) slide into marginal territory if they drop further down the order. Furthermore, we continue to manage the absence of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith**, both of whom remain on the IL. With no viable healthy replacements on the bench, our focus remains on minimizing risk with **Geraldo Perdomo** (55.93), who continues to provide necessary stability in the middle infield while we await the return of our injured stars.",
